---
import DocLayout from '../../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
---

<DocLayout title="Layout" description="Content-first widths, page structure, and layout guidance for building with Farn">
  <h1>Layout</h1>
  <span class="badge badge-beta">beta</span>
  <p>
    Farn's layout philosophy is content-first: let the content determine the container size, not
    the other way around. Width tokens give you three semantic slots. Structural HTML gives you
    meaningful landmarks. Grid and flex each have a clear job.
  </p>

  <h2 id="widths">Content-first widths</h2>
  <p>
    Three width tokens cover the full range of layout needs. Apply them to the element that owns
    the constraint — usually a wrapper <code>&lt;div&gt;</code> with <code>margin-inline: auto</code>.
  </p>

  <div class="width-demo">
    <div class="width-bar width-bar--content">
      <span class="width-label"><code>--width-content</code></span>
      <span class="width-value">1080px · outer container</span>
    </div>
    <div class="width-bar width-bar--narrow">
      <span class="width-label"><code>--width-narrow</code></span>
      <span class="width-value">640px · forms, dialogs</span>
    </div>
    <div class="width-bar width-bar--prose">
      <span class="width-label"><code>--width-prose</code></span>
      <span class="width-value">70ch · running prose</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    <code>70ch</code> is relative to the element's own font size, so prose columns naturally
    widen slightly for display headings and narrow for captions — no extra math required.
    For the full spacing reference including padding scale and z-index, see
    <a href="/styles/spacing">Styles &rsaquo; Spacing</a>.
  </p>

  <div class="accordion">
    <details>
      <summary>Width token reference</summary>
      <div class="accordion-panel">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Token</th>
              <th>Value</th>
              <th>Use</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><code>--width-content</code></td>
              <td><code>1080px</code></td>
              <td>Outer page container — navigation, hero, section wrappers</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>--width-prose</code></td>
              <td><code>70ch</code></td>
              <td>Text column — articles, docs, any running prose</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>--width-narrow</code></td>
              <td><code>640px</code></td>
              <td>Tight containers — forms, dialogs, focused card layouts</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>

  <h2 id="structure">Page structure</h2>
  <p>
    Use semantic landmarks. The wireframe below shows a typical page skeleton and the natural
    width token pairing for each landmark.
  </p>

  <div class="wireframe">
    <div class="wf-header">
      <span class="wf-label">header</span>
      <span class="wf-token">max-width: var(--width-content)</span>
    </div>
    <div class="wf-body">
      <div class="wf-main">
        <span class="wf-label">main</span>
        <span class="wf-token">max-width: var(--width-content)</span>
        <div class="wf-article">
          <span class="wf-label">article</span>
          <span class="wf-token">max-width: var(--width-prose)</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="wf-aside">
        <span class="wf-label">aside</span>
        <span class="wf-token">var(--width-narrow)</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="wf-footer">
      <span class="wf-label">footer</span>
      <span class="wf-token">max-width: var(--width-content)</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="accordion">
    <details>
      <summary>Page structure code</summary>
      <div class="accordion-panel">
        <pre><code>&lt;body&gt;
  &lt;header&gt;
    &lt;!-- max-width: var(--width-content) --&gt;
    &lt;nav&gt;...&lt;/nav&gt;
  &lt;/header&gt;

  &lt;main&gt;
    &lt;!-- outer bound: var(--width-content) --&gt;

    &lt;article&gt;
      &lt;!-- prose column: var(--width-prose) --&gt;
      &lt;h1&gt;...&lt;/h1&gt;
      &lt;p&gt;...&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;/article&gt;

    &lt;aside&gt;
      &lt;!-- sidebar or supplemental: var(--width-narrow) --&gt;
    &lt;/aside&gt;
  &lt;/main&gt;

  &lt;footer&gt;
    &lt;!-- max-width: var(--width-content) --&gt;
  &lt;/footer&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;</code></pre>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>

  <h2 id="grid-flex">Grid vs flex</h2>
  <p>
    Flex for one-dimensional alignment, grid for two-dimensional layout. The demo below uses
    <code>repeat(auto-fill, minmax(180px, 1fr))</code> — columns appear as space allows,
    collapsing to a single column on narrow viewports without a media query.
  </p>

  <div class="grid-demo">
    {[1, 2, 3, 4].map(n => (
      <div class="grid-demo-card" data-surface="layer">
        <span class="grid-card-label">Card {n}</span>
        <p class="grid-card-meta">Grid auto-fill</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="accordion">
    <details>
      <summary>Grid vs flex pattern reference</summary>
      <div class="accordion-panel">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Pattern</th>
              <th>Use</th>
              <th>Example</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Flex row</td>
              <td>Aligning items along a single axis</td>
              <td>Nav links, button group, icon + label</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Flex column</td>
              <td>Stacking with controlled spacing</td>
              <td>Form fields, card body</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Grid columns</td>
              <td>Placing items in explicit rows and columns</td>
              <td>Card grid, two-column doc layout</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Grid auto-fill</td>
              <td>Responsive columns without breakpoints</td>
              <td><code>repeat(auto-fill, minmax(240px, 1fr))</code></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>
          Always use <code>gap: var(--space-*)</code> rather than margins between grid or flex children.
          This keeps spacing in the token system and avoids margin-collapse edge cases.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>

  <h2 id="radius">Radius as hierarchy</h2>
  <p>
    Border radius is not purely decorative — it signals depth and interactivity. Use the scale
    consistently so elements at the same depth read as related.
  </p>

  <div class="radius-demo">
    <div class="radius-box" style="border-radius: var(--radius-sm)">
      <code>--radius-sm</code>
      <span>4px · badges, code</span>
    </div>
    <div class="radius-box" style="border-radius: var(--radius-md)">
      <code>--radius-md</code>
      <span>6px · buttons, inputs</span>
    </div>
    <div class="radius-box" style="border-radius: var(--radius-lg)">
      <code>--radius-lg</code>
      <span>8px · cards, panels</span>
    </div>
    <div class="radius-box" style="border-radius: var(--radius-xl)">
      <code>--radius-xl</code>
      <span>12px · hero cards</span>
    </div>
    <div class="radius-box" style="border-radius: var(--radius-full)">
      <code>--radius-full</code>
      <span>9999px · pills</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    Nest radii correctly: an inner element should have a smaller radius than its container,
    roughly <code>container-radius - padding</code>. Matching radii at every level makes nested
    surfaces look misaligned. See <a href="/styles/spacing">Styles &rsaquo; Spacing</a> for the
    full radius token reference.
  </p>

  <h2 id="z-index">Stacking order</h2>
  <p>
    Eight z-index tokens define a predictable stacking ladder. Never hardcode z-index values —
    use the tokens so layers stay relative to each other as the system grows.
  </p>

  <div class="z-demo">
    <div class="z-layer z-base">
      <code>--z-base · 0</code>
      <span>Normal flow</span>
    </div>
    <div class="z-layer z-raised">
      <code>--z-raised · 1</code>
      <span>Floated cards</span>
    </div>
    <div class="z-layer z-content">
      <code>--z-content · 10</code>
      <span>Sticky sub-nav</span>
    </div>
    <div class="z-layer z-dropdown">
      <code>--z-dropdown · 100</code>
      <span>Dropdowns, popovers</span>
    </div>
    <div class="z-layer z-sticky">
      <code>--z-sticky · 200</code>
      <span>Sticky header</span>
    </div>
    <div class="z-layer z-overlay">
      <code>--z-overlay · 300</code>
      <span>Modal backdrop</span>
    </div>
    <div class="z-layer z-modal">
      <code>--z-modal · 400</code>
      <span>Modal dialog</span>
    </div>
    <div class="z-layer z-toast">
      <code>--z-toast · 500</code>
      <span>Toasts, notifications</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    The stacking order matches the visual hierarchy: page content sits at the bottom, transient
    UI (toasts, modals) at the top. Never set a dropdown above a modal — if a component needs to
    break this order, the design decision is worth questioning first.
  </p>
</DocLayout>

<style>
  /* ── Width demo ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .width-demo {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .width-bar {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    background: var(--color-bg-panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .width-bar::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: var(--color-accent);
    opacity: 0.08;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }

  .width-bar--content { width: 100%; }
  .width-bar--narrow  { width: min(100%, 640px); }
  .width-bar--prose   { width: min(100%, 70ch); }

  .width-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--color-text);
    white-space: nowrap;
    position: relative;
  }

  .width-value {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    position: relative;
  }

  /* ── Wireframe ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .wireframe {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
  }

  .wf-header,
  .wf-footer,
  .wf-main {
    background: var(--color-bg-panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-md);
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .wf-header,
  .wf-footer {
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
  }

  .wf-body {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .wf-main {
    flex: 1;
    flex-direction: column;
    min-height: 120px;
  }

  .wf-article {
    flex: 1;
    background: var(--color-bg-inset);
    border: 1px dashed var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    padding: var(--space-sm);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .wf-aside {
    width: 140px;
    background: var(--color-bg-panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-md);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) /* --breakpoint-mobile */ {
    .wf-body { flex-direction: column; }
    .wf-aside { width: auto; }
  }

  .wf-label {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .wf-token {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: 11px;
  }

  /* ── Grid demo ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .grid-demo {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(180px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .grid-demo-card {
    padding: var(--space-md);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background: var(--color-bg);
  }

  .grid-card-label {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .grid-card-meta {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  /* ── Radius demo ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .radius-demo {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .radius-box {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 100px;
    background: var(--color-bg-panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding: var(--space-md) var(--space-sm);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .radius-box code {
    font-size: 11px;
    background: none;
    padding: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .radius-box span {
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
  }

  /* ── Z-index demo ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .z-demo {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .z-layer {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    border-left: 3px solid;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-accent) var(--_z-bg), transparent);
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-accent) var(--_z-border), transparent);
  }

  .z-layer code {
    background: none;
    padding: 0;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--color-text);
    white-space: nowrap;
    min-width: 160px;
  }

  .z-layer span {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .z-base     { --_z-bg:  4%; --_z-border:  20%; }
  .z-raised   { --_z-bg:  7%; --_z-border:  30%; }
  .z-content  { --_z-bg: 10%; --_z-border:  40%; }
  .z-dropdown { --_z-bg: 13%; --_z-border:  50%; }
  .z-sticky   { --_z-bg: 16%; --_z-border:  60%; }
  .z-overlay  { --_z-bg: 20%; --_z-border:  70%; }
  .z-modal    { --_z-bg: 24%; --_z-border:  80%; }
  .z-toast    { --_z-bg: 28%; --_z-border: 100%; }

  @media (max-width: 640px) /* --breakpoint-mobile */ {
    .z-layer { flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .z-layer code { min-width: unset; }
  }
</style>
